{
  "name": "Loire turret",
  "_about": "A LOIRE CORNER TURRET (Chenonceau's, Azay-le-Rideau's): a round shaft (`sides`, R, H tall, `t` walls) standing on a cul-de-lampe `cor` deep under its foot (three rings narrowing down -- corbelled out from a corner), belt courses at the house's floors (h1, h1 + h2 over its foot), a small window with a moulded frame in face 0 (+z: yaw it to look out) on each floor, a corbelled cornice corOut proud, a tall slate cone capRise high from capR at its eave, a lead finial. Place its foot at the house's ground floor, its +z out along the corner's diagonal.",
